# Compiled binaries
#
# `go build ./...` in a module with a main package writes the binary into the
# current directory, so the real output lands at desktop/zenith rather than
# anywhere near the old cli/zenith guess. Both are listed, and /bin/ below
# covers the conventional build directory.
cli/zenith
desktop/zenith
quickshell/quickshell

# Build artifacts
build/
*.o
*.a
*.so

# Python bytecode
#
# system/verify-packages.py is the only Python in the repository and is run as a
# script, so it never needs a compiled cache. One was committed before this rule
# existed — a build of an older revision of that script, which is the worst kind
# of stale file to carry because it looks current and runs silently.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Go build artifacts
/bin/
/pkg/
/tmp/

# IDE and editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
*.swo

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Coding agent files, local only.
#
# Every one of these is a machine-local pointer or per-tool configuration. None
# of them is reviewed, none belongs in the repository, and committing one
# leaks a contributor's editor layout into a project that has no opinion about
# it.
#
# The contract they point to, agents/agents.md, stays tracked. It is the master
# agent contract and the design system, CONTRIBUTING and the pull request
# template both bind contributors to it, and the CI workflows cite it as the
# source of the commands they run. Only the pointers are machine-local.
#
# AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md are symlinks to agents/agents.md, so each
# name needs its own entry — a symlink is matched by its own path, not by what
# it points at. Keep this list anchored to the repository root: a bare
# `AGENTS.md` would also hide `system/agents.md` and `agents/agents.md`'s
# siblings in any subtree, which is how a real source file goes missing.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md

# Generated diagram output. The HTML is a build artifact of the archify tool,
# not a source file; the candidate JSON next to it is the thing worth keeping.
.archify/

# Per-tool agent and assistant configuration, same reasoning.
.cursorrules
.cursor/
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.windsurfrules
.aider*
.mcp.json
.cline/
.continue/
.codex/
.ampproject/

# Binaries written by `go build` inside a cmd directory
desktop/cmd/*/zenith-agent
desktop/cmd/*/zenith-hubd
desktop/cmd/*/zenith-shell
desktop/cmd/*/zenith-wallpaper
desktop/cmd/*/zenith-store
desktop/cmd/*/zenith-vm
desktop/cmd/zenith/zenith
/→/
